WEBVTT

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:07.560
"Did you cross the sea, too?"

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:13.130
The sea... A blue gemstone? An aquamarine?

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.850
No, didn't Richard say...

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.790
<i>It means "the blue that came
 from beyond the sea."</i>

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.310
That was...

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.210
<i>It's sometimes called ultramarine.</i>

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.200
Lapis lazuli!

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.590
Here it is! This is it.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.020
Nakata-kun?

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:57.470
It's here.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
<u>Episode 10</u>
<b>The Lapis Lazuli of Guidance</b>

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.140
<i>It's inlaid with lapis lazuli on all sides...</i>

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.980
<i>The Standard of Ur.</i>

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.310
You fool.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.260
Richard!

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.100
I'll lecture you later.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.190
Airport, please.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.610
What are you thinking?

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:20.060
Sorry.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.830
I didn't ask for an apology.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:24.760
Well, I'm really, truly sorry!

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.470
Hey, calm down. Are you all right?

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.580
Oh, pardon me.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:32.940
Seigi?

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.380
Seigi, what's wrong?

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.950
You're awake.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:45.850
Where are we?

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:53.380
Your fever seems to have come down a little.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:56.430
I don't remember what happened 
after we got in the taxi.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:04:00.700
You began losing consciousness and 
would only say you were all right.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:06.300
We stopped at a nearby hotel, and I was 
just thinking about calling a doctor.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.270
Really, I'm fine now.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.060
Yes, you've said that a hundred times.

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.310
I'm surprised you knew we were there.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:20.690
The photos he uploaded to social media 
were following his old walking route.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:23.820
Then shouldn't we hurry up
 and get out of here?

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.920
Stay put. You still need to rest.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.990
Why are you here?

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:33.540
I paid you more than the salary you were owed.
You should have nothing to complain about.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:40.810
Richard, please... Don't disappear 
on me without saying a word.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:46.120
When you left, I felt like 
a hole opened in my chest.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:47.890
I couldn't do anything.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:51.270
There are some things that talking can't fix.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.320
You didn't have to tell me why.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:55.570
Just that you were going to London.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.810
Why would I need to tell you that?

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.610
Why?

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:05.470
Just like you've done for me, 
if you're in trouble, I...

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:08.460
It's much more useful 
for you not to be here.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:09.830
Go home.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:13.870
Trying to be too good will destroy you.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:17.460
I could say the same to you.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:21.050
Why did he leave that will, anyway?

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.160
Surely it didn't have to be so mysterious.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.990
Perhaps there's no distinct 
reason behind the malice.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:30.670
I suppose he was displeased with everything.

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:33.730
His son running away, 
the death of his family...

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:37.580
Perhaps it was spite that made 
the seventh Count Claremont

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:41.860
want to restore the purity 
of his family bloodline.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:49.740
And you fought with Jeffrey and broke 
up with your boyfriend because of it?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.240
What?

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:52.200
What?

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:58.460
I've never had a male lover. Okay?

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.420
Okay...

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:08.430
It seems you're confused, 
but she was a Turkish Englishwoman.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.050
I see.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.010
So what are you going to do now?

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:18.500
I have no obligation to honor the 
hatred of a man who died alone.

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:22.730
I will continue to run for as long as I must.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:24.110
Run?

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:27.260
It's what I've done for four years.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:28.950
I'm used to solitude.

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:32.440
Once you've recovered, 
you'll go to the airport

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:35.250
and take the earliest flight back to Tokyo.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.250
Understood?

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:40.400
And then you'll vanish from my life forever?

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:43.540
You still haven't responded to my request.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:54.030
Seigi...

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.470
I crossed the ocean to get here, too.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.190
I'm surprised you thought I'd 
figure out that meant lapis lazuli.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:04.320
If you'd forgotten, then that's 
all it would've meant to you.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:05.770
Richard, I—

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:06.820
Go home.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:10.010
A student's job is to study.

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:13.120
You're far too young to be sticking 
your nose into the affairs of adults.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:15.450
You really are...

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:23.520
Are you there? Do you hear me?

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:25.130
Henry.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:26.510
Huh?

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:29.840
What's that?

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.180
What's this doing here?

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:45.690
<i>Are you there, Nakata-kun? It's Jeffrey.</i>

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:51.380
<i>It seems my phone ended up
 in your bag somehow.</i>

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:56.250
<i>But thanks to its GPS functionality, 
I was able to track it down.</i>

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:57.650
Track?

00:07:57.650 --> 00:08:00.780
<i>My lawyer contacted me.</i>

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:05.240
<i>To cut to the chase, you weren't 
on the unacceptable list.</i>

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:07.010
What? That means...

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:09.560
<i>You're a viable marriage candidate.</i>

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:11.460
<i>Congratulations!</i>

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:14.620
<i>So, Nakata-kun, will you help me?</i>

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:18.590
I warned you to stay out of my life!

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:25.350
They're only interested 
in inheriting the diamond.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:29.610
You don't need to listen to them.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:35.670
Seigi, we'll leave through the balcony.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:40.160
Mr. Nakata... Please, save Richard.

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:41.630
Please...

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.730
The nonsense of a ghost. 
Don't listen to him.

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:47.740
But...

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:06.520
Seigi!

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:14.490
Henry?

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:18.990
Yes... Please save Richard.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:25.350
Harry...

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:28.710
Nakata-kun, have you considered my offer?

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:31.500
Seigi is just an employee. 
Don't get him involved.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:34.300
I'll help you.

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:37.730
That's great.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:38.930
Seigi!

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:43.560
So what do I have to do,
and how much are you paying me for it?

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:04.120
My lawyer confirmed that forming a 
civil partnership with an Asian person

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.420
wasn't prohibited by the list.

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:08.440
A civil partnership?

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:11.880
It's a legally recognized partnership 
between a same-sex couple,

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:15.350
equivalent to a heterosexual marriage.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.600
Won't we need to register?

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:21.440
Don't worry. With both Richard 
and his potential spouse present,

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:23.330
the diamond will be released.

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:26.430
Then, once you're married, it'll be all yours.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.940
What do you say to splitting 
the 300 million pounds evenly?

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.550
That makes about 20 billion yen...

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:33.110
It'll be taxed, won't it?

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:35.290
We'll take care of that.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:39.320
You know, I think you and I are 
going to be great friends.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:50.640
You're so cold, Your Highness. 
You should look happier.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:53.420
Your lover is willing to pitch in

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.340
to potentially free us from 
this troublesome curse.

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:59.100
He's just being shy.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:53.940
Read this later.

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:22.760
Seigi! Don't do it!

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.010
That gemstone is—

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.650
What happened? Nakata-kun!

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:52.960
It's a white sapphire.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:55.960
It's not a diamond.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.440
It's not... a diamond?

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:11.790
<i>The truth behind the cursed will was 
hidden in that bundle of old letters.</i>

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:19.030
<i>Dear Father, I received your kindness.</i>

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:21.640
<i>My heart will always be with you.</i>

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:24.000
<i>From Sri Lanka, with Leah.</i>

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:29.700
<i>My beloved son, 
you must not return to England.</i>

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.490
<i>If you come home with Leah,</i>

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:37.240
<i>the foolish white supremacists will 
inflict unbearable humiliation upon you.</i>

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:44.980
It wasn't the seventh count who opposed 
our grandfather's marriage, but the family.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:47.760
Then why did he disown him?

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:51.520
Likely to deceive the family.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:56.400
Our great-grandfather probably bought 
the sapphire pretending it was a diamond,

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:00.630
and sent his son the difference 
in price as a gift before his death.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.630
At the time, this sapphire's market price

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:05.860
was probably tens of thousands of pounds.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:08.840
Not a 30-million-pound diamond,

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:11.790
but a white sapphire worth only 
tens of thousands of pounds...

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:14.450
So why did he leave that will?

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:18.290
It was probably his revenge
 against the racists who tried

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:20.080
to block his son's marriage.

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:21.670
His revenge?

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:27.060
Originally, only their descendants 
would've been bound by the will.

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:30.430
But the air raids threw everything off...

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.930
He who hurts another hurts himself.

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:38.030
It's a saying that means 
if you try to harm another,

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:41.100
you bring harm upon yourself, too.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:45.530
It was his beloved son's descendants 
who fell into this cursed trap.

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:49.230
In other words, us.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:02.040
Uh, I guess I'm going to the police?

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.480
That won't be necessary.

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:07.430
It wasn't a diamond.

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:09.550
More importantly...

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:13.510
Nakata Seigi, you don't understand anything.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:14.810
Huh?

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:16.830
Why did you write this?

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:22.940
Pudding Recipe

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:22.940
It's the recipe for the pudding 
I always made for you.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:24.720
Why give that to me?

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:29.590
Allow me to answer for you.

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:31.910
You learned working at Étranger

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:38.480
that diamonds are hard, but easily 
broken with directional pressure.

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:43.390
In order to nullify the will, 
you planned to shatter the diamond,

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:47.290
shoulder the blame, 
and disappear from my life.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:48.760
Am I wrong?

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:51.280
I made up my mind yesterday...

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:55.010
Whoever's with you can make pudding for you.

00:15:55.700 --> 00:16:01.030
Do you take me for a man who'd presume 
on your kindness and then abandon you?

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:03.680
Did you think that would make me happy?

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:04.850
Behave yourself.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:10.880
You once said you were afraid of 
disappointing your loved ones

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:13.410
because you couldn't do anything for them.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:16.240
When you talk of a "hero of justice,"

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:19.620
you mean a useful tool to 
be used in a time of need.

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:25.150
In other words, the deep-seated 
reason for your reckless behavior

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:27.710
is that sense of powerlessness 
that torments you.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.960
The last time we met, I told you

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:37.720
that you didn't need to be 
a hero of justice anymore.

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:42.550
Your desire to be useful is admirable,

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:46.230
but Seigi, your life belongs to you.

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:53.030
I don't want you to become a useful tool.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:56.740
I want you to remain my 
dear friend Nakata Seigi.

00:16:57.710 --> 00:17:04.000
The people who love you all 
want you to be happy, Seigi.

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:09.290
And it goes without saying 
that I'm one of those people.

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:29.620
Are you hungry?

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:33.790
Oh, no.

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:35.400
I'm leaving tomorrow,

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:38.290
so I'm making pudding to apologize 
to Richard and thank him.

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.120
Pudding?

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:42.510
Oh, that brings back memories.

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:45.330
Our governess used to make it for us.

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:47.010
Governess?

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:51.100
Our tutor. She'd make it for us as a reward.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:53.300
I see.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:56.840
Anyway, you got me.

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.950
The power of love is incredible, Nakata-kun.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:03.430
You're quite the Japanese man.

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:07.420
You fooled a native from 
the country of Shakespeare.

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:10.230
Oh, right, that...

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:13.270
But if you'd actually broken the diamond,

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:17.320
he probably would've spent 
the rest of his life atoning to you,

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:20.450
or even said he'd prefer 
to bear the blame with you.

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:22.990
I wouldn't want him to do that.

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:24.540
I see.

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:27.930
I actually wanted to apologize.

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:30.000
I'm sorry, Nakata-kun.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:33.750
I also tried to use you, you know.

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:36.870
I'm glad Richard has you.

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:40.090
He doesn't need anyone other 
than me making him unhappy.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:44.850
It doesn't have to be right away, 
but please talk to Richard.

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:21.510
Well done. Have some pudding.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.900
The governess's pudding?

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:44.060
I've had it almost a hundred times.

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:47.330
So this time, I offer some to you...

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.830
Though I would honestly prefer not to.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:56.750
What I desire now is to see you well.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:04.340
Let's eat, Harry and Jeff.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:08.430
Thanks, Ricky.

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:18.070
This is your ticket for today.

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:23.400
So, what are you going to do once 
everything with the inheritance is settled?

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:25.860
I haven't decided yet.

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:27.260
I see.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.690
That's...

00:20:32.740 --> 00:20:36.200
I want you to hold on to this white sapphire.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:37.380
What? But...

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:40.550
There's too much history wrapped up inside it.

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:44.720
I'd like you to keep it and drive that out.

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:48.480
I've already spoken with my family.

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.730
It's not fair if I'm the only
one getting something.

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:57.250
I want you to have this.

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:02.440
I can't accept that. 
It belonged to your grandmother.

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:04.580
Then let's do this:

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:09.450
when I return your sapphire to you, 
you can return this to me.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:12.120
Very well.

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:15.910
Then let's make it the last 
time you and I meet.

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:16.710
What?

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:20.490
As long as we have these gemstones,

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:23.700
whether we become civil 
servants or mafia bosses,

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:26.380
get married or fall ill,

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:29.850
we must always remain in touch.

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:33.220
Even if it's decades from now.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:36.060
Got it.

00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:27.960
Saul-san, I bought red bean jelly.

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:32.010
Good morning, Seigi.

00:23:34.110 --> 00:23:36.010
You're here rather early.
